jepa-platonic-toy demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/jepa-platonic-toy/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment
toy inspired by:

  Balestriero, LeCun,
  "Proving and Improving the Platonic Representation Hypothesis with JEPAs",
  Brown University / New York University / AMI Labs, arXiv:2610.39302
  (October 2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.39302
  https://arxiv.org/html/2610.39302v1
  https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.39302

Found via a bookmarked X post by @HuggingPapers:
  https://x.com/HuggingPapers/status/2116804737207021735
  (thread with https://x.com/HuggingPapers/status/2116804727228784718)

Paper verified on arXiv and Hugging Face Papers on 2026-11-02. Official
code (https://github.com/galilai-group/prh-proof) and demo Space
(https://huggingface.co/spaces/galilai-group/prh_demo) exist but are
**not vendored**. This app is an **independent clean-room toy** of
good-view JEPA cross-modal alignment on a synthetic finite world — NOT a
reproduction of the paper's Flickr / COCO / Recap-DataComp / 70B LM tables.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Trained weights stay out of git (work/ is
git-ignored).
